{
  "summary": "Based on the documented rates and your $5,000 balance, the strongest fit appears to be a Gold Account paired with a Gold Rewards Card, provided you qualify for the card and already have—or are willing to pay for—the required Rho-Bank+ subscription.",
  "recommended_combination": {
    "savings_account": "Gold Account",
    "credit_card": "Gold Rewards Card",
    "why": [
      "The Gold Account earns a documented 5.5% APY.",
      "Its normal $10,000 minimum-balance requirement is reduced to $5,000 when paired with a Gold Rewards Card.",
      "The Gold Rewards Card adds a documented 0.025 percentage-point APY bonus to the Gold Account.",
      "The Gold Rewards Card has a $0 annual fee and earns 2.5% cash back on purchases.",
      "Light Blue checking does not appear in the documented list of checking accounts that provide a savings APY boost, so keeping it should not add a documented boost to this plan."
    ],
    "estimated_savings_interest": {
      "assumed_average_balance": "$5,000",
      "effective_documented_rate": "5.525% APY",
      "approximate_one_year_interest_before_other_fees": "$276.25"
    },
    "important_costs": [
      "The Gold Rewards Card requires an active Rho-Bank+ subscription; the subscription price was not provided in the available product information.",
      "The Gold Account may charge a $10 monthly maintenance fee if the balance falls below $10,000, although the Gold Rewards Card benefit reduces the required minimum to $5,000. Keep the balance at or above $5,000.",
      "The Gold Account documentation says internal transfer fees may apply, so confirm the funding fee before moving the $5,000.",
      "To avoid credit-card interest, pay the card statement balance in full each month. The purchase APR is 17.99% if you carry a balance."
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "combination": "Gold Account plus EcoCard",
      "assessment": "Not ideal for a $5,000 savings balance.",
      "reason": "The EcoCard provides a larger documented Gold Account APY bonus of 0.6%, but it does not document the $10,000-to-$5,000 minimum-balance reduction. At $5,000, the Gold Account could therefore incur its monthly fee or fail its normal balance requirement."
    },
    {
      "combination": "Silver Plus Account plus EcoCard",
      "assessment": "Potentially suitable if you do not qualify for Gold Rewards or do not want Rho-Bank+.",
      "reason": "The Silver Plus Account requires a $5,000 minimum balance and the EcoCard provides a documented 0.45 percentage-point APY bonus. However, the available documents contain inconsistent Silver Plus base-rate information, so I cannot calculate a reliable one-year net return for this option."
    }
  ],
  "credit_card_rewards_note": "Savings interest is based on your $5,000 balance. Credit-card cash back depends on how much you spend; it is additional value rather than interest on the savings deposit. The Gold Rewards Card's 2.5% cash back would equal about $25 per $1,000 of eligible purchases, assuming you pay the balance in full.",
  "next_step": "Before opening anything, confirm whether you have Rho-Bank+ and its monthly price, whether your average balance will stay at least $5,000, and whether you expect to spend enough on the card to benefit from cash back. I can then calculate the net one-year estimate more precisely."
}
